== 1.8 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Money is best defined as anything that is],
  [generally acceptable in payment of goods and debts],
  [issued by a government],
  [kept in a bank],
  [made of paper or metal]
)

#mcq(2, [The direct exchange of goods for goods is],
  [commerce],
  [barter only in villages],
  [barter],
  [trade]
)

#mcq(3, [Barter requires a double coincidence of],
  [wants],
  [prices],
  [incomes],
  [seasons]
)

#mcq(4, [The function of money that ends the need for a double coincidence of wants is],
  [store of value],
  [measure of value],
  [medium of exchange],
  [standard of deferred payment]
)

#mcq(5, [When a trader writes a price of ₦500 on a shirt, money is acting as a],
  [standard of deferred payment],
  [store of value],
  [measure of value],
  [medium of exchange]
)

#mcq(6, [A worker who keeps part of his salary in a bank for December is using money as a],
  [measure of value],
  [medium of exchange],
  [standard of deferred payment],
  [store of value]
)

#mcq(7, [A loan repayable in twelve months' time illustrates money as a],
  [measure of value],
  [medium of exchange],
  [store of value],
  [standard of deferred payment]
)

#mcq(8, [Which of these is money but NOT legal tender?],
  [a ₦1,000 note],
  [a ₦1 coin],
  [a bank current account balance],
  [a ₦50 note]
)

#mcq(9, [Legal tender is],
  [a cheque],
  [any money],
  [a credit card],
  [coins and notes that a creditor must accept in settlement]
)

#mcq(10, [A cheque is],
  [legal tender],
  [an order to a bank to pay from an account],
  [commodity money],
  [fiat money]
)

#mcq(11, [The quality of money that allows it to be carried about is],
  [durability],
  [divisibility],
  [homogeneity],
  [portability]
)

#mcq(12, [Cattle are a poor money chiefly because they lack],
  [acceptability],
  [value],
  [divisibility],
  [scarcity]
)

#mcq(13, [Yams are unsuitable as money mainly because they lack],
  [scarcity],
  [durability],
  [portability],
  [divisibility]
)

#mcq(14, [The quality that makes one unit of money exactly like another is],
  [scarcity],
  [homogeneity],
  [durability],
  [portability]
)

#mcq(15, [Money that holds its purchasing power over time is said to have],
  [stability of value],
  [portability],
  [homogeneity],
  [divisibility]
)

#mcq(16, [Near money is],
  [money in a pocket],
  [an asset that can quickly be turned into money at little loss],
  [money owed to a bank],
  [foreign currency only]
)

#mcq(17, [Cowries used in the old West African trade are an example of],
  [fiat money],
  [commodity money],
  [electronic money],
  [bank money]
)

#mcq(18, [Paper money that is not backed by gold but is money because the law says so is],
  [near money],
  [convertible paper money],
  [commodity money],
  [fiat money]
)

#mcq(19, [A balance in a current account that moves by cheque is],
  [commodity money],
  [legal tender],
  [fiat money],
  [bank money]
)

#mcq(20, [A balance held in a mobile wallet and spent by transfer is],
  [commodity money],
  [electronic money],
  [legal tender],
  [near money]
)

#mcq(21, [Narrow money (M1) consists of currency in circulation plus],
  [demand deposits],
  [savings deposits],
  [time deposits],
  [treasury bills]
)

#mcq(22, [Broad money (M2) is larger than narrow money because it adds],
  [government debt],
  [foreign reserves],
  [coins],
  [savings and time deposits]
)

#mcq(23, [In rapid inflation, money performs the store-of-value function badly because],
  [the notes wear out],
  [its purchasing power falls],
  [it ceases to be legal tender],
  [banks close]
)

#mcq(24, [The difficulty of barter that is solved by a common unit of account is],
  [the risk of theft],
  [the double coincidence of wants],
  [the absence of a measure of value],
  [the lack of portability]
)

#mcq(25, [Cigarettes used as money in a prison camp show that money depends on],
  [metal content],
  [general acceptability],
  [legal tender status],
  [government issue]
)

#mcq(26, [Which is NOT a function of money?],
  [medium of exchange],
  [measure of value],
  [production of goods],
  [store of value]
)

#mcq(27, [Which is NOT a quality of good money?],
  [perishability],
  [durability],
  [portability],
  [divisibility]
)

#mcq(28, [A treasury bill held by a firm is best described as],
  [near money],
  [money],
  [capital],
  [legal tender]
)

#mcq(29, [A credit card is],
  [a means of obtaining credit],
  [near money],
  [money],
  [legal tender]
)

#mcq(30, [Cowries served as money in West Africa because they were],
  [issued by the colonial government],
  [backed by gold],
  [generally acceptable, durable and divisible],
  [difficult to transport]
)

#mcq(31, [The form of money with the greatest liquidity is],
  [currency in circulation],
  [a bill of exchange],
  [a treasury bill],
  [a fixed deposit]
)

#mcq(32, [Gold coins circulated as money for centuries mainly because gold is],
  [light],
  [plentiful],
  [divisible, durable and scarce],
  [cheap]
)

#mcq(33, [Convertible paper money is a note that],
  [cannot be exchanged],
  [may be exchanged for a fixed weight of gold],
  [has no value],
  [is issued by a commercial bank]
)

#mcq(34, [The largest component of the modern money supply in most countries is],
  [notes],
  [bank deposits],
  [coins],
  [foreign currency]
)

#mcq(35, [When the same good is used both for consumption and as money, the good is],
  [commodity money],
  [near money],
  [electronic money],
  [fiat money]
)

#mcq(36, [Money solves the problem of deferred payment because it],
  [is issued by the central bank],
  [has a fixed value in law],
  [is portable],
  [provides a unit in which a future debt can be fixed]
)

#mcq(37, [Which statement about money is correct?],
  [foreign currency is legal tender in Nigeria],
  [all money is legal tender],
  [cheques are legal tender],
  [all legal tender is money]
)

#mcq(38, [An increase in the general price level reduces the],
  [purchasing power of money],
  [acceptability of money],
  [portability of money],
  [divisibility of money]
)

#mcq(39, [The four functions of money are medium of exchange, measure of value, store of value and],
  [unit of production],
  [source of revenue],
  [standard of deferred payment],
  [means of taxation]
)

#mcq(40, [The double coincidence of wants is a difficulty of],
  [advertising],
  [insurance],
  [banking],
  [barter]
)

